        {
          "question": "q-333430",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=4{x}^{2}\\sqrt{y},\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $\u0394x=0.5,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current values $x$ and $y?$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056690/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "5ac140158747f1464abf6af2f63553af74a620f7d11ad2416483fa46e562b707"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1836,
