    {
      "question": "e-21679",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/problem",
      "old_sha256": "d8f98760ea1cc16781e3f86f379ac2149339243fc8ac2db70638225ba9641efa",
      "new_sha256": "c90c1afe4e3bf30016804714615c4919633378b0290e2cd41e1fa7515b3ab1be",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-21679",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny' = 2y^2 - \\sqrt{x}, \\qquad y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $\\Delta x = 1,$ the new value $y_\\text{new}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g(y_\\text{new}) = 0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **specific function** $g(y_\\text{new})$ used in the first step?\n\n- $g(y_\\text{new}) = y_\\text{new} - (y_\\text{new})^2 - 1 + \\dfrac12\\sqrt{2}$\n\n- $g(y_\\text{new}) = y_\\text{new} - \\dfrac12 (y_\\text{new})^2 - \\dfrac32 + \\dfrac12\\sqrt{2}$\n\n- $g(y_\\text{new}) = y_\\text{new} - (y_\\text{new})^2 - \\dfrac32 + \\dfrac12\\sqrt{2}$\n\n- $g(y_\\text{new}) = y_\\text{new} - (y_\\text{new})^2 - \\dfrac32 - \\dfrac12\\sqrt{2}$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056690/example-21679.json",
          "file_sha256": "bb23e3182a02d476b071f192971797df053eb7a2cb6c9abba8bf3ac1a9908154"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1836,
