    {
      "question": "e-21679",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "e47cd50110a4cca54b29168ea60e5d7c0a7b91a472f0ec26644bc14bb5b1132a",
      "new_sha256": "06a8e7e60ec0e56ce1e9f4fcb6dffd1a143718499ab247fc4bc9cbb9f46bc919",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-21679",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\ny' = f(x,y), \\qquad y(a) = c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $\\Delta x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\Delta y = \\dfrac12(y' + y'_\\text{new}) \\cdot \\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwith $y'_\\text{new} = f(x_\\text{new},y_\\text{new})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $\\Delta y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394y & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{\u2032}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{\u2032})\\cdot \u0394x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2{y}^{2}-\\sqrt{x}+2({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{x}+({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into $y_\\text{new} = y + \\Delta y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\u0394y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{x}+({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{{x}_{\\text{new}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMoving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\ny_\\text{new} - (y_\\text{new})^2 - y - y^2 + \\dfrac12\\sqrt{x} + \\dfrac12\\sqrt{x_\\text{new}} = 0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $\\Delta x = 1$ is\n\n$$\ng(y_\\text{new}) = y_\\text{new} - (y_\\text{new})^2 - y - y^2 + \\dfrac12\\sqrt{x} + \\dfrac12\\sqrt{x_\\text{new}}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\nx_\\text{new} = x + \\Delta x = 1 + 1 = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-1-{1}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{1}+\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14056690/example-21679.json",
          "file_sha256": "bb23e3182a02d476b071f192971797df053eb7a2cb6c9abba8bf3ac1a9908154"
        }
      ],
